      "servingTime": "25-30 minutes",
      "yield": "4-6 servings",
      "tips": "",
      "ingredients": "For the Sweet Mayo Sauce:\n1/4 cup. mayonnaise\n2 tbsps. sweetened condensed milk\nFor the Sandwich:\n2 tbsps. vegetable oil\n1 can of Royal Smokehouse Chicken Luncheon Meat, sliced into thick pieces\n4 large eggs\n2 tbsps. heavy cream\nsalt and pepper to taste\n2 tbsps. butter\n6 slices brioche bread\n6 pcs. cheddar cheese slices\n2 tbsps. spring onions, chopped\nFor the Sweet Mayo Sauce:\n1/4 cup. mayonnaise\n2 tbsps. sweetened condensed milk",
      "procedure": "In a small bowl, whisk together the mayonnaise and sweetened condensed milk. Set the sauce aside.\nHeat a pan over medium-high heat then add vegetable oil. Place the sliced Royal Smokehouse Chicken Luncheon Meat and pan-fry for 2-3 minutes per side, until golden brown and slightly crispy. Remove from the pan and set aside.\nIn a bowl, whisk the eggs with the heavy cream, season with salt, and pepper until well combined. \nIn the same pan, melt 1 tablespoon of butter over medium-low heat. Pour in the egg mixture. Gently scramble the eggs, using a spatula to push and fold them until they form large, fluffy curds. Don't overcook them; they should still be a little moist.\nMelt the remaining tablespoon of butter in the pan. Place the thick-cut bread slices in the pan and toast on both sides until golden and crispy.\nPlace one toasted bread slice on a plate. Top the half part of the bread with fluffy scrambled eggs.\nAdd one slice of cheese over the egg. The warmth of the bread will help it melt.\nPlace a slice of the fried Royal Smokehouse Chicken Luncheon Meat on top of the cheese slice.\nGenerously drizzle the sweet mayo sauce over the fillings and Sprinkle with chopped spring onions.\nClose the sandwich with the other half of toasted bread. Serve while still warm."
