      "procedure": "Pat the tofu cubes dry with a paper towel. \nHeat the cooking oil in a small pan over medium-high heat. Carefully place the tofu cubes in the pan and fry until golden brown and crispy on all sides. Remove the tofu and set it aside on a paper towel-lined plate to drain excess oil.\nBring the water to a boil in a pot.\nAdd Hana Dried Pollock Ramen and cook for 3-4 minutes, or according to the package instructions.\nAdd the ramen soup base, dried vegetable flakes, and soy sauce to the pot. Stir to combine.\nAdd the bean sprouts, carrots, bell pepper, shiitake mushrooms, and bok choy to the pot. \nCook for another 1-2 minutes until the vegetables are slightly softened but still have a bit of a crunch.\nRemove from the heat and add sesame oil. \nCarefully pour the cooked noodles, broth, and vegetables into a large ramen bowl.\nArrange the fried tofu cubes on top of the ramen. Garnish with chopped spring onions and serve immediately."
